{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$6x^2+5x-1$ defines a polynomial function.\n\nPolynomial functions are continuous across their entire domain, and their domain is all real numbers.\n\nIn other words, for any polynomial $p$ and any possible input $c$, we know that this equality holds:\n\n$\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to c}p(x)=p(c)$\n\nTherefore, in order to find $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to -1}(6x^2+5x-1)$, we can simply evaluate $(6x^2+5x-1)$ at $x=-1$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}6x^2+5x-1\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=6(-1)^2+5(-1)-1\\qquad\\gray{\\text{Substitute }x=-1}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=6-5-1\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=0\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to -1}(6x^2+5x-1)=0$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to -1}(6x^2+5x-1)=$ [[☃ numeric-input 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"numeric-input 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"maxError":null,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":0}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"Input answer","size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
